IPC anointment live-plane scenario driver.

live-scenarios.sh runs the acceptance matrix from
docs/ipc-anointments-design.md ("Scenarios") against a running capability
plane: session reach for the shipped tiers, anoint(1) elevation (driven
through a real pty because anoint reads readpassphrase(3)/RPP_REQUIRE_TTY),
the non-admin su authenticated mint, and a graph --lint check that the base
tree carries no dead declaration or duplicate endpoint.

It is deliberately not a kyua test: it needs a live plane, real local
accounts, and passwords set before the auth agent starts.  Run it by hand on a
disposable VM.  scenario-policy.ucl is the principal policy it expects.  The
header of live-scenarios.sh has the full one-time setup.

Requires the tests package (service_probe, pty_askpass under /usr/tests).
